NAME
       xargs - build and execute command lines from standard input

SYNOPSIS
       xargs [-0rt] [-n N] [-I STR] [-d DELIM] [COMMAND [ARG]...]

DESCRIPTION
       Read items separated by blanks and newlines from standard input and run
       COMMAND (default echo) with the items appended as arguments. Quotes and
       backslashes in the input are honored.

OPTIONS
       -n N
           use at most N items per command line

       -I STR
           run COMMAND once per input line, replacing STR in the arguments

       -0
           items are separated by NUL characters (see find -print0)

       -d DELIM
           items are separated by DELIM

       -r
           do not run COMMAND if the input is empty

       -t
           print each command line before running it

EXAMPLES
       find . -name '*.o' | xargs rm
       ls *.c | xargs -I{} cp {} /root/backup/

SEE ALSO
       find(1)
